# Verification

Done is a claim: a command exited 0 on this tree.

Cursor does not run Claude Code hooks. Follow the same agreement anyway, and do not treat a missing hook as permission to skip the checks.

- Run `python3 .verify/verify_runner.py` before you call a task done.
- Do not write a PASS verdict by hand.
- Do not edit `.claude/`, `.verify/`, `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `REVIEW.md`, or `.cursor/rules/`.
- Do not modify or delete an existing test, and do not add a skip. New tests are allowed.
- Stay inside the active brief. If a file is not on its allowed list, leave it alone.
- CI on the protected branch is the lock. A local editor rule is only a reminder.

`CLAUDE.md` is the Claude Code copy of this rule. `AGENTS.md` is the Codex copy. The done sentence is the same in all three.
